    <text>
        <body>
            <div>
                <head>Translated parts</head>
                <p xml:id="CH1e0877-start">
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:07:18.751+09:00">Seventh year, spring, second month, jihai (day 36).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:09:49.714+09:00">Xianqiu was set on fire.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:10:03.917+09:00">What does “set on fire” mean?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:10:11.832+09:00">To burn with firewood.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:10:46.14+09:00">What does “to burn with firewood” mean?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:10:54.834+09:00">It means to use fire to launch an attack.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:11:11.126+09:00">What is implied by “using fire to launch an attack”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:11:44.191+09:00">It is an expression of disdain at the first instance of using fire to launch an attack.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:11:58.96+09:00">What is Xianqiu?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:12:11.548+09:00">It was a Zhulou settlement.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:12:19.938+09:00">Why is it not associated with Zhulou?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:12:34.887+09:00">To present it as the capital.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:12:48.813+09:00">Why present it as the capital?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:13:01.921+09:00">Simply because the ruler was residing there.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:46:13.198+09:00">Ninth year, spring.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:46:34.879+09:00">Ji Jiang of Ji was sent to her marital home in the Royal Capital.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:14.227+09:00">If the wording “Queen” of the previous record “gives full realization” to the fact that for the King there is no Exterior,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:38.803+09:00">why does this record designate her as “Ji Jiang of Ji”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:46.071+09:00">From our Lu perspective we speak in Ji’s voice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:06.76+09:00">When Ji parents refer to their daughter,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:19.118+09:00">even though she has become Heaven’s Queen,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:36.557+09:00">they would still call her “our Ji Jiang.”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:12.404+09:00">so the wording of the record gives full realization to this! </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:27.049+09:00">For the King there is no “Exterior”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:41.361+09:00">In this case, why is she called “Queen”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:57.007+09:00">When a bride is in her natal state she is called “daughter”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:15.799+09:00">Therefore, if we approved of acting as a go between, then the great officer could, on the basis of our approval, use this approval to proceed on to Ji to meet the bride.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:06.321+09:00">The Son of Heaven directed us to act as a go between.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:33.466+09:00">In what way did the completion of his mission depend on us?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:49.439+09:00">The completion of his mission depended on us.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:04.833+09:00">In this case, why does the record say “subsequently”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:19.143+09:00">A great officer must not initiate a subsequent undertaking.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:31.67+09:00">It indicates an ensuing undertaking.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:47.036+09:00">What does “subsequently” indicate?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:53:05.164+09:00"> In the ritual of marriage, the groom is not designated.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:01.06+09:00">Who is the Duke of Zhai?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:15.818+09:00">He was one of the Three Ministerial Dukes of the Son of Heaven.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:31.684+09:00">Why is he not designated as being dispatched?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:55:32.615+09:00"> The Duke of Zhai came.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:55:41.113+09:00">Subsequently, he went to receive the Queen in Ji.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:58:43.578+09:00">Ninth month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:58:57.108+09:00">The Marquis of Qi escorted Lady Jiang to Huan.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:59:08.151+09:00">Why was the record made?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:59:19.128+09:00">To criticize.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:59:31.168+09:00">What is criticized by this?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:59:49.425+09:00">Regional lords crossing state borders to escort a bride,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:00:06.94+09:00">violate ritual propriety.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:00:18.915+09:00">Since she had in fact entered the state of Lu,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:00:33.772+09:00">why not designate her as “the lord’s wife”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:00:53.228+09:00">From our Lu perspective we speak in Qi’s voice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:01:08.592+09:00">When Qi parents refer to their daughter,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:01:25.355+09:00">they would continue to call her “Our Lady Jiang”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:01:46.798+09:00">even though she has become the lord’s wife from a neighboring state.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:01.946+09:00">Ninth month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:13.515+09:00">Ji Liexu came to receive the bride.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:25.892+09:00">Who is Ji Liexu?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:38.508+09:00">He was a great officer of Ji.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:47.106+09:00">Why is he not designated as being “dispatched”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:03:59.668+09:00"> In marriage rituals no reference is made to the groom.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:04:20.598+09:00">If so, to whom are references made?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:04:40.053+09:00">References are made to the father, elder brothers, teachers, and friends.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:05:07.7+09:00">Then why is there a reference to the groom in the record “The Duke of Song dispatched Gongsun Shou to come to present betrothal gifts”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:05:22.14+09:00">The possibility of a ritual pronouncement had been exhausted.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:05:40.99+09:00">Why had the possibility of a ritual pronouncement been exhausted?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:05:56.139+09:00">There was no groom’s mother to make the ritual pronouncement.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:06:10.687+09:00"> If so, was there no mother of the Ji’s groom to make the ritual pronouncement?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:06:23.273+09:00">It is said that there was.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:06:31.154+09:00">If there was, why is no reference made to this mother?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:06:46.925+09:00">Mothers’ doings are not communicated.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:07:27.481+09:00">When a state of the Exterior receives a bride, it is not recorded.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:07:44.47+09:00">In this case, why is it recorded?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:07:54.83+09:00">To criticize.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:08:07.509+09:00">What is criticized by this?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:08:19.149+09:00">The record criticizes the first instance of not welcoming the bride in person.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:08:33.31+09:00">Did the first instance of not welcoming the bride in person occur on this occasion?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:08:44.322+09:00">It had occurred before this.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:08:55.932+09:00">If it had occurred before this, then why is it presented as the first occasion here?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:09:08.953+09:00">It is simply treated as the first occasion.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:09:15.508+09:00">Why simply treat it as the first occasion?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:09:31.311+09:00">It is the first occasion in the Chunqiu.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:10:07.197+09:00">Why is a daughter of Lu sometimes referred to as “bride”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:10:19.582+09:00">sometimes referred to as “wife”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:10:33.316+09:00">and sometimes referred to as “the lord’s wife”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:10:46.636+09:00">When a daughter is in her natal state she is called “bride”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:10:57.496+09:00">when she is on the road, she is called “wife”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:11:05.586+09:00">and when she enters her new marital home state she is called “the lord’s wife”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:12:05.376+09:00">Third month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:12:18.193+09:00">The lord joined by Yifu of Zhulou swore a covenant at Mie.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:12:23.617+09:00">What does ji (及) mean?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:12:43.61+09:00">It means yu (與), “to join together”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:12:50.648+09:00">Hui (會), ji (及), and ji (暨) all mean yu (與), “to join together”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:24:40.375+09:00">So why does the record sometimes say hui (會),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:13:16.556+09:00">sometimes say ji (及),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:13:22.703+09:00">and sometimes say ji (暨)?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:13:53.524+09:00">Hui (會) is like zui (最), meaning “to gather together”;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:14:09.805+09:00">ji (及) is like jiji (汲汲), meaning “pressing”;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:14:15.024+09:00">and ji (暨) is like  jiji (暨暨), meaning “resolutely”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:14:30.692+09:00">so ji (及) indicates that we desired the encounter</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:15:05.306+09:00">and ji (暨) indicates that we had no choice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:02.929+09:00"> Someone from Jin seized the Marquis of Wei</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:27:57.413+09:00">What does “returned him to” indicate?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:08.773+09:00">and returned him to the Royal Capital.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:35.629+09:00">What does “he was returned to” indicate?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:46.745+09:00">“Returned him to” indicates guilt had already been determined;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:08.048+09:00">“He was returned to” indicates guilt had not yet been determined.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:39.096+09:00">So why, in another record, where the guilt has not yet been determined, could the seizing qualify as an overlord’s punishment?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:52.39+09:00">“Returned him to” (in the present record) indicates</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:07.296+09:00">that a person was seized at the behest of the Son of Heaven,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:21.166+09:00">so whether or not he was determined to be guilty,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:34.971+09:00">can be deduced.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:51.994+09:00">“He was returned to” (in the other record)</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:12.063+09:00">indicates that a person was not seized at the behest of the Son of Heaven,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:21.889+09:00"> so whether or not he was determined to be guilty,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:39.662+09:00">cannot be deduced.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:03.933+09:00">What was the Marquis of Wei’s crime? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:11.04+09:00">He killed Shuwu.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:41.359+09:00">Why was this not recorded? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:51.722+09:00">To respectfully conceal the killing for the sake of Shuwu. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:01.826+09:00">The Chunqiu conceals for the sake of the worthy. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:09.643+09:00">What was worthy about Shuwu? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:21.385+09:00">He yielded the state. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:27.94+09:00">How is it that he yielded the state?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:04.062+09:00">Lord Wen of Jin expelled the Marquis of Wei and installed Shuwu. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:23.262+09:00">If Shuwu had declined to be installed and another had been established in his stead, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:33.877+09:00">he feared that the Marquis of Wei would not be able to return. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:47.202+09:00">Consequently, Shuwu set himself up as lord</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:57.437+09:00"> and subsequently availed himself of the meeting at Jiantu to manage the return of the Marquis of Wei to his state. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:07.997+09:00">After the Marquis of Wei had been able to return,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:41.476+09:00">“Shuwu usurped my position.” </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:30.418+09:00">he declared,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:52.433+09:00">Yuan Xuan disputed this, saying, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:04.207+09:00">“Shuwu is innocent!”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:14.757+09:00">In the end, the Marquis of Wei killed Shuwu </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:29.605+09:00">and Yuan Xuan fled and left the state. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:58.277+09:00">This was Marquis of Jin, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:08.714+09:00">why does it designate him as “someone”? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:16.808+09:00">To degrade him. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:25.329+09:00">Why degrade him? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:34.215+09:00">The disaster in Wei was Lord Wen’s creation. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:42.826+09:00">How did Lord Wen precipitate it? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:52.331+09:00">When Lord Wen of Jin expelled the Marquis of Wei to install Shuwu, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:02.891+09:00">he caused an elder and younger brother of another state to suspect one another, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:11.84+09:00">effecting the murder of a maternal younger brother. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:16.898+09:00">It was Lord Wen of Jin who did this!</seg>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
